<https://w3id.org/tvbo/evict> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/tvbo> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/evict> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "evict" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/evict_equation
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/evict_equation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/evict_equation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/evict_equation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "evict_equation (slot)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/evict_equation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Optional reverse recurrence for a **sliding-window** reduction: the per-step downdate that removes the sample leaving the window, the inverse of ``equation`` (which folds an arriving sample in). Only meaningful when ``equation_type: recurrence`` on an observation's auxiliary ``dynamics``. When present, the observer is a windowed reduction — its state is maintained by ``equation`` (add) and ``evict_equation`` (evict) and rebuilt exactly from the window on resync — rather than a cumulative accumulator over the whole trajectory (``equation`` alone). Absent for ordinary state variables and cumulative reductions." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/evict_equation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/tvbo> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/evict_equation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "evict_equation" .
