<https://w3id.org/tvbo/node_selection> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "node_selection" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/node_template
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/node_template> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/node_template> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/node_template> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "node_template (slot)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/node_template> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Default Node attributes applied to every Node in this Network. Explicit entries in `nodes:` override the template field-by-field (shallow replace, same semantics as `dict.update`). The per-Node slots (id, label, position, region) come from the data backbone (Network.iri-loaded parcellation or procedural generator) and are no template slots, so a template that sets one is refused, naming it. Lets a homogeneous Network declare its per-Node configuration once without enumerating regions." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/node_template> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/tvbo> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/node_template> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "node_template" .
