<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Assignment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "One step of a sequential recurrence: the expression assigned to a target name. Sequential rather than simultaneous — a later step's expression sees the value the steps above it assigned — which is what lets a reducer's update be authored as ordinary arithmetic instead of with `new_*` temporaries. Authored terse as a `[target, expression]` pair and lifted to this form on load." .
