<https://w3id.org/tvbo/CouplingStageEvaluation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/CouplingStageEvaluation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/CouplingStageEvaluation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "CouplingStageEvaluation" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/CouplingStageEvaluation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "How the network coupling term is evaluated within one step of a multi-stage integrator (Heun, RK4, ...). A backend-neutral numerical contract: whether the coupling is part of the vector field, re-evaluated at each solver stage, or computed once per step and held constant across the stages. Matters because the two choices integrate a different effective system — for stiff / chaotic / multistable dynamics they can converge to different trajectories or attractors." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/CouplingStageEvaluation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/tvbo> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/CouplingStageEvaluation> <https://w3id.org/linkml/permissible_values> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/CouplingStageEvaluation#per_stage> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/CouplingStageEvaluation> <https://w3id.org/linkml/permissible_values> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/CouplingStageEvaluation#per_step> .
