<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Document> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Document> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Document" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Document> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The envelope of a record written as its own file. ``tvbo_class`` names the class the file holds and ``schema_version`` the schema it was written against; both are facts about the file, so TVBO's dialect drops them before construction and no object ever carries them. Declaring them here is what lets a third party validate a TVBO file with plain ``linkml-validate``. A class taking this mixin pins its own CURIE with ``slot_usage: {tvbo_class: {equals_string: ...}}``, so a file naming the wrong class is refused natively." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Document> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/common> .
