<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Mesh> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Mesh> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Mesh" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Mesh> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Triangle (or higher-order) mesh geometry. May stand alone (via ``mesh_file`` pointing at an external GIFTI/VTK/MSH file) OR be inlined on a Network as ``Network.mesh``. In the inlined-on-Network case, the vertices are the parent Network's ``nodes/coordinates`` (so ``coordinates`` here may be left empty), the faces live in the same h5 companion under a path given by ``elements`` (default ``mesh/faces``), and optional per-vertex ``normals`` / ``curvature`` live alongside. The optional ``parcel_map_field`` points at the parent Network's per-vertex parcel-id array (default ``nodes/parent_index`` from the hierarchical-Network pattern, see Network.qmd §7.1)." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Mesh> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/Mesh> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Mesh> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/tvbo> .
