<https://w3id.org/tvbo/PanelKind> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "What a panel draws. cartesian/heatmap are grammar-driven (mark + encoding); surface paints a layer on a mesh, volume projects one through a labelled volume and network draws one on a node-link graph; grid tiles a composite of sub-panels; colorbar/legend are shared keys in their own slot; image (external file) and custom (registered callable) are peer escape-hatch kinds. A new kind is added when its bsplot leaf exists." .
