<https://w3id.org/tvbo/PropagationGate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> _:genid3302 .
_:genid3302 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#maxCardinality> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger> .
_:genid3302 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/min_dispersion> .
_:genid3302 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/PropagationGate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/PropagationGate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "PropagationGate" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/PropagationGate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A propagation requirement on a grouped wave reduction. A per-timestep wave test cannot tell a standing field from a travelling one, since a standing field repeats the same spatial pattern every timestep. The reduction sums the per-element unit direction vector over the post-transient timesteps and computes each group's direction dispersion, the ``mask``-weighted mean over elements of 1 - |time-mean direction|: 0 for a direction field fixed in time, growing as the direction moves. A group whose dispersion falls below ``min_dispersion`` has no travelling waves, so its proportion of waves is 0 and its proportion-directed and rho are undefined (NaN)." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/PropagationGate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/PropagationGate> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/PropagationGate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/tvbo> .
