<https://w3id.org/tvbo/ReferenceFingerprint> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Cache-invalidation fingerprint for one ``aux_data`` reference. Captures enough about the upstream artifact that a downstream cache can decide cheaply (via mtime + size) whether to trust the cached result, falling back to a hash recompute on mismatch." .
