# https://w3id.org/tvbo/CouplingStageEvaluation#per_stage
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/CouplingStageEvaluation#per_stage> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/CouplingStageEvaluation#per_stage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/CouplingStageEvaluation> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/CouplingStageEvaluation#per_stage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/CouplingStageEvaluation#per_stage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "per_stage (CouplingStageEvaluation)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/CouplingStageEvaluation#per_stage> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "per_stage" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/CouplingStageEvaluation#per_stage> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "recompute_coupling_per_stage" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/CouplingStageEvaluation#per_stage> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Re-evaluate the coupling at every integrator stage, as part of the vector field: standard ODE integration, and what a reference integrator of a stiff, chaotic or multistable network computes. tvboptim's native solvers honour it as recompute_coupling_per_stage=True, NetworkDynamics.jl integrates this way natively, and the jax backend re-evaluates an undelayed coupling at each stage's state and refuses it over a delayed one, whose history read it cannot shift to a stage's time. TVB and the Python graph runner compute the coupling once per step, so they refuse it wherever it changes the system integrated: a multi-stage method over more than one node. tvboptim's diffrax solvers and PyRates integrate this way whatever is declared." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/CouplingStageEvaluation#per_stage> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "per_stage" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/CouplingStageEvaluation#per_stage> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "per-stage coupling evaluation"@en .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/CouplingStageEvaluation#per_stage> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Re-evaluate the network coupling term at every stage of a multi-stage integrator. Costlier, but the coupling seen by each stage is consistent with that stage's state; the difference from per-step matters for stiff or chaotic coupled networks."@en .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/CouplingStageEvaluation#per_stage> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/backendParameter> "tvboptim: recompute_coupling_per_stage=True" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/CouplingStageEvaluation#per_step
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/CouplingStageEvaluation#per_step> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/CouplingStageEvaluation#per_step> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/CouplingStageEvaluation> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/CouplingStageEvaluation#per_step> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/CouplingStageEvaluation#per_step> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "per_step (CouplingStageEvaluation)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/CouplingStageEvaluation#per_step> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "per_step" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/CouplingStageEvaluation#per_step> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Evaluate the coupling once per integration step and hold it across the step's stages, the TVB scheme: the coupling reduction runs once per step, at the cost of an order of accuracy in the coupling, which can move a sensitive system onto another trajectory. TVB and the Python graph runner always integrate this way, and the jax backend and tvboptim's native solvers do as their default (recompute_coupling_per_stage=False on tvboptim). NetworkDynamics.jl holds each vertex's summed input on parameters that a callback sets at the start of every step, for every multi-stage method, adaptive ones included, and refuses it together with execution.find_fixpoint. tvboptim's diffrax solvers and PyRates re-evaluate the coupling at every stage whatever is declared." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/CouplingStageEvaluation#per_step> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "per_step" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/CouplingStageEvaluation#per_step> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "per-step coupling evaluation"@en .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/CouplingStageEvaluation#per_step> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Evaluate the network coupling once per integration step and hold it frozen across the integrator's stages. The default, and the classic TVB treatment."@en .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/CouplingStageEvaluation#per_step> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/backendParameter> "tvboptim: recompute_coupling_per_stage=False" .
