# https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#from_branch
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#from_branch> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#from_branch> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#from_branch> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#from_branch> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "from_branch (InitialStateMethod)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#from_branch> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Start from a point on a previously computed branch. No continuation backend implements it: a continuation declaring it is refused by name before anything renders or runs. A continuation from a special point of another is declared as a branch of that continuation instead (Continuation.branches, with its BranchSwitch.source_point)." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#from_branch> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "from_branch" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#from_experiment
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#from_experiment> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#from_experiment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#from_experiment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#from_experiment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "from_experiment (InitialStateMethod)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#from_experiment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Seed from the settled endpoint state of another already-run experiment in the study (referenced by InitialState.source_experiment). Reuses a working point that experiment already reached instead of recomputing it — the cross-experiment counterpart of from_working_point (which recomputes the ramp inline). source_point selects which settled point of the source run (default 'endpoint')." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#from_experiment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "from_experiment" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#from_working_point
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#from_working_point> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#from_working_point> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#from_working_point> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#from_working_point> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "from_working_point (InitialStateMethod)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#from_working_point> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Ramp a parameter quasi-statically (warm-start / from_previous) to a target value (see InitialState.ramp) and start from the endpoint state — reach a working point on the solution branch before the run." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#from_working_point> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "from_working_point" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#given
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#given> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#given> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#given> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#given> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "given (InitialStateMethod)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#given> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Start from the model's declared initial values as they are. A continuation takes them as its starting equilibrium on every continuation backend, and refuses a state whose right-hand side exceeds InitialState.abs_tol in any component, since AUTO-07p would start its branch at a state that is not an equilibrium and BifurcationKit would correct it first; newton finds the equilibrium near such a state." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#given> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "given" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#newton
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#newton> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#newton> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#newton> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#newton> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "newton (InitialStateMethod)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#newton> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Start from the equilibrium Newton's method converges to from the model's declared initial values: SciPy's root by MINPACK's hybr, to a relative step of InitialState.abs_tol, refused where it does not converge. Resolved once, before any backend runs, so every continuation backend starts from the same state; on a network every node starts from it." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#newton> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "newton" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#time_integration
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#time_integration> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#time_integration> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#time_integration> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#time_integration> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "time_integration (InitialStateMethod)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#time_integration> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Integrate the model from its declared initial values for InitialState.duration and start from the state it reaches. The default of a continuation, on every continuation backend." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/InitialStateMethod#time_integration> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "time_integration" .
