# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/PanelKind#grid
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/PanelKind#grid> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/PanelKind#grid> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/PanelKind> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/PanelKind#grid> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/PanelKind#grid> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "grid (PanelKind)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/PanelKind#grid> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A composite of sub-panels inside ONE lettered panel, labelled once per row and column. What a paper's lettered panel usually is: a row of mode surfaces under a single (a), or a Data/Reconstruction matrix whose task name is written once at the left. Declaring each cell as its own mosaic entry instead would repeat those labels in every cell and renumber panels the paper letters once. Cells come from `cells:` or, in the common case, from `layers:` — one cell per layer, all drawn by the shared `cell:` template." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/PanelKind#grid> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "grid" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/PanelKind#heatmap
