<https://w3id.org/tvbo/ParallelMode#lax_map> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Sequential execution via jax.lax.map. Slower; bounded memory." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/ParallelMode#lax_map> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "lax_map" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/ParallelMode#pmap
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/ParallelMode#pmap> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/ParallelMode#pmap> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/ParallelMode> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/ParallelMode#pmap> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/ParallelMode#pmap> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "pmap (ParallelMode)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/ParallelMode#pmap> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Parallel execution across the local devices of a single node (jax.pmap over the several GPUs/TPUs visible to that task). Intra-task only — it never spans nodes; inter-node parallelism is scheduler fan-out (DistributionConfig.chunk), not pmap. On a one-GPU (or CPU) task this degenerates to vmap." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/ParallelMode#pmap> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "pmap" .
# 
