# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepSeeding#from_previous
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepSeeding#from_previous> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepSeeding#from_previous> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepSeeding> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepSeeding#from_previous> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepSeeding#from_previous> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "from_previous (SweepSeeding)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepSeeding#from_previous> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Each point is seeded from the final state of the preceding point, so the trajectory follows the solution branch as the swept parameter changes quasi-statically. Forces sequential, order-dependent execution (emitted as a scan, not a vmap). Used to reach a working point by slowly ramping a parameter (e.g. global coupling) and, with sweep_direction, to expose hysteresis / multistability. The sweep-granularity form of InitialStateMethod.from_working_point, which ramps a parameter to one working point." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepSeeding#from_previous> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "from_previous" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepSeeding#independent
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepSeeding#independent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepSeeding#independent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepSeeding> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepSeeding#independent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepSeeding#independent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "independent (SweepSeeding)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepSeeding#independent> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Points are order-independent and may be evaluated in parallel (see parallel_mode). Default. Independent of each OTHER, which is not the same as each cold-starting: where the experiment declares a transient, the settle is integrated once and every point opens from the state it reached, so what is shared between points is a settled state rather than a running trajectory. That is sound while the swept parameter does not change the approach, and unsound wherever the sweep crosses a bifurcation, since a point then inherits an attractor it would not have reached on its own. The emitter integrates one settle, not one per point, so the name promises independence between points, not a cold start at each." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepSeeding#independent> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "independent" .
