<https://w3id.org/tvbo/study/Cohort> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/study/Cohort> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Cohort (study)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/study/Cohort> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A named subset of a dataset's subjects: the unit a group-level quantity is defined over, such as a mean connectome, a per-edge presence count or a normalisation constant. A dataset may hold several, and they may overlap: the sites of a multi-centre study, a patient and a control group, the subjects a processing pipeline has finished so far. Naming the subset is what pins an aggregate. A quantity computed over ``hcpy93`` states which subjects went into it, and moving to a larger cohort is a change to one identifier rather than to every consumer." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/study/Cohort> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/study> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/study/Cohort> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "Cohort" .
