_:genid4733 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/study/CohortRule> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/study/CohortRule> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "CohortRule (study)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/study/CohortRule> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Admits a cohort's members by a measure of a phenotype table: the candidates are cut into ``n_groups`` groups along ``measure`` and the cohort holds the group ``group``. The candidates are the members of the cohort ``of`` names, else the subjects the dataset lists, else every subject of the table. Each candidate needs one row in the table. A candidate without a row, or whose value is missing or not finite, is treated as ``missing`` says, before any group is formed. The members come in the candidates' order, not in the order of the measure. A group no candidate falls in is an error, as a cohort without members is." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/study/CohortRule> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/study> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/study/CohortRule> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "CohortRule" .
