<https://w3id.org/tvbo/models/SupHopf> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Supercritical Hopf (SUPH) is an oscillatory/excitable neural mass model that describe the normal form of a supercritical Hopf bifurcation in Cartesian coordinates (Kuznetsov, 2013; Deco et al., 2017). \n\nThis normal form has a supercritical bifurcation at 'a=0' with 'a' the bifurcation parameter in the model. So for 'a < 0', the local dynamics has a stable fixed point and the system corresponds to a damped oscillatory state, whereas for 'a > 0', the local dynamics enters in a stable limit cycle and the system switches to an oscillatory state." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/models/SupHopf> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/studies/Deco2017> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/models/SupHopf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/models/SupHopf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "SupHopf" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/models/SupHopf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Supercritical Hopf"@en .
