# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_hrf_strided
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_hrf_strided> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_hrf_strided> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/Observation> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_hrf_strided> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "BOLD fMRI observation model identical to BOLD_TVB's HRF+Volterra forward model, but with the HRF convolution and TR subsampling fused into a single strided convolution (strided_convolve): the convolution is evaluated only at the retained [stride::stride] output samples, avoiding the full-length FFT. Byte-identical to a direct full 'valid' convolution + subsample; equal to the FFT path to FFT roundoff (~1e-12 float64 / ~1e-6 float32); ~70x cheaper with no FFT buffer." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_hrf_strided> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/studies/Schirner2023> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_hrf_strided> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_hrf_strided> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "BOLD_HRF_strided" .
