# https://w3id.org/tvbo/software/vbi
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/software/vbi> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/software/vbi> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/sw/SimulationTool> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/software/vbi> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Virtual Brain Inference. Probabilistic inference toolkit for whole-brain models — multi-backend simulators (Numba, C++, CuPy, JAX, PyTorch, TVB kernels), a 40+ time-series feature library (statistical, spectral, FC/FCD, complexity, event-detection), and two parallel inference paths (SBI via sbi-toolkit SNPE/SNLE/SNRE with MAF/NSF, and a built-in autograd-based CDE with MDN/MAF estimators). Targets the inverse problem of mapping observed neuroimaging (EEG/MEG/fMRI) onto brain-model parameters." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/software/vbi> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> "MIT" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/software/vbi> <http://schema.org/codeRepository> "https://github.com/ins-amu/vbi" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/software/vbi> <http://schema.org/identifier> "10.5281/zenodo.14795543" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/software/vbi> <http://schema.org/url> "https://vbi.readthedocs.io" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/software/vbi> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/software/vbi> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "vbi" .
