<https://w3id.org/tvbo/number_of_nodes> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Number of nodes in the network, derived from `nodes` when it lists them. Beside a source (an `iri`, a `data_file`, a `bids_dir` or the curated network of a `parcellation`) it is the number of the source's nodes the network keeps: all of them at the source's own count, and below it a random subset drawn once at build from `execution.random_seed`, which `node_selection` then names. A count above the source's is refused." .
