<https://w3id.org/tvbo/symmetric> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Centre the limits on zero, so zero is the map's midpoint. What a field of signed deviations needs — read on an off-centre scale it is misleading in a way no axis label catches." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/symmetric> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/figure> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/symmetric> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "symmetric" .
# 
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/symmetry> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/symmetry> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "symmetry (slot)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/symmetry> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Declared symmetry of the edge function: 'directed' (default), 'antisymmetric', or 'symmetric', shown in reports. Every backend evaluates each direction of a connection as its own directed edge, so it changes no simulation." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/symmetry> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/tvbo> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/symmetry> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "symmetry" .
# 
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/tail_samples> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> .
