<https://w3id.org/tvbo/tail_samples> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Number of samples from the end to use. Takes the last N samples before aggregation. E.g., tail_samples: 500 means use data[-500:]. Prefer `tail_duration` when the window means a duration — a sample count silently rescales when the step size changes. On an algorithm's observation it must fit within one `simulation_period`; a window across iterations is a `tail_duration`." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/tail_samples> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/tvbo> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/tail_samples> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "tail_samples" .
