# 
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/unicode_minus> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/unicode_minus> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "unicode_minus (slot)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/unicode_minus> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Write a negative number with a true minus sign rather than a hyphen." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/unicode_minus> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/figure> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/unicode_minus> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "unicode_minus" .
# 
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/unit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/unit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "unit (slot)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/unit> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Physical unit of measurement. `UnitEnum` is the curated vocabulary — each of its values is vendored from QUDT (`ontology/tvb-o-units.ttl`) and can be reasoned about dimensionally. The range is deliberately open beyond it: a unit nobody has curated yet is recorded as written and reported `uncurated`, because a closed range forces the author to either misdeclare the quantity or leave it undeclared, and both lose more than an unrecognised string does. An uncurated unit carries no dimensional claim, so a check involving it reports `underdetermined` rather than guessing. Promote one with `tvbo units add <unit>`, which pulls its QUDT record into the vendored module — so every unit TVBO *reasons* about stays authoritative, and only what it *records* is open." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/unit> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/tvbo> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/unit> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "unit" .
# 
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/used> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/used> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "used (slot)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/used> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A labelled array sourced from another experiment's result, a dataset, or a curated entity — the cross-container form of a value (WHERE + WHICH + SLICE, PROV ``prov:used``). Mutually exclusive with ``value``; an in-study ``experiment`` reference also registers the workflow dependency so the source runs first. Resolved lazily, never inlined into generated code." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/used> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Bind the annotation to a scalar in a result container (same reference form a Layer uses, and the same PROV edge). The referenced value is formatted through `text` at render time, so a statistic printed on a panel is computed, never transcribed." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/used> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Bind the key to a computed scalar in a result container (same reference form a figure Layer uses, and the same PROV edge). Mutually exclusive with ``value`` and ``count``." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/used> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "IRIs of the inputs, outputs and environment the activity consumed (BEP028 ``Used``)." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/used> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The p-value, a scalar in a result container (same reference form a Layer uses, and the same PROV edge)." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/used> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "WHERE + WHICH + SLICE for a template edge whose whole matrix is read rather than stored or computed: another network's layer, an analysis result, or a cohort member's own connectome (``used: {cohort: <id>, query: {...}, output: weight, reconcile: by_label}``). Inside a per-subject run a cohort reference resolves to that run's subject, which is what binds a model network to each subject's own connectivity. ``reconcile: by_label`` aligns the read matrix to this network's node order through its atlas aliases. Resolved lazily and never inlined, and it wins over a same-named layer in the companion file. Mutually exclusive with ``producer:``." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/used> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "WHERE + WHICH + SLICE in one edge — this parameter's array sourced from another experiment's result (an operating point, a tuned ``estimate__<name>`` a fit persisted), a dataset, or a curated entity, PROV ``prov:used``. The full cross-container form of which `source:`+`measure:` is the no-``sel``/no-``experiment`` shorthand; adds label ``reconcile`` and a swept-point ``sel``. Like `source:` the array is resolved lazily and never inlined. An in-study ``experiment`` reference also registers the workflow dependency. Mutually exclusive with `value:`/`source:`/`producer:`." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/used> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#used> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/used> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/tvbo> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/used> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/figure> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/used> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "used" .
