# 
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/study/of> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/study/of> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "of (study)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/study/of> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "``cohort_id`` of another cohort of the same dataset whose members are the candidates, so a split is taken inside a cohort. That cohort may itself be typed, read from a file or admitted by a rule; a chain that leads back to this cohort is an error." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/study/of> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/study> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/study/of> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "of" .
# 
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/study/opaque> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/tvbo.owl> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/study/opaque> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "opaque (study)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/study/opaque> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "BIDS: the standard does not specify the contents, so a validator does not read inside. A sanctioned opaque directory therefore needs no ``.bidsignore`` entry however its files are named." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/study/opaque> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/study> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/study/opaque> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "opaque" .
